CertiStack check: is this controller ready for certistack plan?
The layers run in order and it stops at the first that fails. Layers 4 to 6 and 8 use a temporary worker on the node, removed afterwards.

  ✓ 1. Environment file  <dir>/controller.env, mode 0600, the 5 required variables are set
  ✓ 2. SSH files         identity <dir>/id_ed25519; <dir>/known_hosts has an entry for [pve-node-01.example.com]:2222
  ✓ 3. SSH connection    ssh to root@pve-node-01.example.com:2222 works without a prompt, with strict host-key checking; the node reports x86_64
  ✓ 4. Node tools        found on the node: qemu-img, proxmox-backup-client, guestfish, ip, nft
  ✓ 5. PVE API           the node reaches the PVE API and PVE accepts the token (Proxmox VE 9.0.3)
  ✓ 6. PBS               the PBS credential lists the repository: 2 VMs have a complete backup
  ✓ 7. Plan              the plan file exists
  ✓ 8. Sandbox network   network.ip_range 192.0.2.0/24 holds neither the PVE API nor the PBS server, and overlaps none of the node's routes or addresses

✓ Every layer passed.
Now run: certistack plan <dir>/my-first-plan.yaml --env-file <dir>/controller.env
